      "relation": {
        "op": "le",
        "left": "len",
        "right": "available - written"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_unicode_escape_must_fit_remaining_space",
      "fine_trace_step": 7,
      "description": "Root cause. On the exact crashing key, byte 15 `0xf2` reaches `const char *str` without unsigned normalization, so `uint32_t c = (uint32_t) str[i];` sign-extends it to `0xfffffff2` and the call takes the `c > 0xFFFF` branch. `flb_utf8_decode()` still resolves bytes `f2 88 88 88` to `0x88208`, so this `snprintf` returns 7 for `\\\\u88208` after only a 6-byte availability check. The patch adds `if ((available - written) < len) return FLB_FALSE;` immediately after this line and duplicates the same obligation at the sibling `\\\\u%.4x` and `\\\\u%.4hhx` escape sites."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_control_escape_copy_sink",
      "role": "sink",
      "file": "src/flb_utils.c",
      "function": "flb_utils_write_str",
      "line": 650,
      "operands": [
        "written"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "eq",
        "left": "written",
        "right": "written"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_overrun_written_reaches_control_escape_sink",
      "fine_trace_step": 10,
      "description": "Closest project sink to the ASan crash. The final control-byte escape copy executes after the remaining-space arithmetic has wrapped, so the `\\\\u0000` write starts at the last in-bounds byte and immediately continues past the end of the original SDS allocation."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_overlong_unicode_escape_copy",
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_unicode_copy_offset_becomes_written_budget",
      "role": "root_cause",
      "file": "src/flb_utils.c",
      "function": "flb_utils_write_str",
      "line": 711,
      "fine_trace_step": 8,
      "state": "The sink-linked `encoded_to_buf(p, tmp, len); p += len;` unicode escape executes with a formatted length that is larger than the remaining checked budget, so the copy advances `p` to the post-escape cursor beyond the budget that the earlier 6-byte precheck assumed.",
      "operands": [
        "(size_t) (p - (buf + *off))",
        "written"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "eq",
        "left": "(size_t) (p - (buf + *off))",
        "right": "written"
      }
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_written_exceeds_available_after_unicode_escape",
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_unicode_copy_offset_becomes_written_budget",
      "role": "intermediate",
      "file": "src/flb_utils.c",
      "function": "flb_utils_write_str",
      "line": 719,
      "fine_trace_step": 9,
      "state": "Immediately after the overlong unicode escape, `written = (p - (buf + *off));` records the post-copy cursor as a value larger than `available`, so later remaining-space arithmetic in the same call wraps instead of rejecting the next escape.",
      "operands": [
        "(size_t) (p - (buf + *off))",
        "written"
      ],
      "relation": {
